    "passage": [
      "An exponential function has the form f(x) = a times b to the power x, with a positive base b not equal to 1. Its key property is that equal steps in x multiply the output by the same factor. A linear function adds a constant amount in each step; an exponential function multiplies by a constant factor. When b is greater than 1 the function grows, and when b is between 0 and 1 it decays.",
      "Exponential growth eventually outpaces any polynomial, however slow it starts. A quantity growing by a fixed percentage per period, such as money at compound interest or an unchecked population, grows exponentially. Its doubling time is constant: if it doubles in 10 years, it doubles again in the next 10. Likewise a radioactive substance has a constant half-life.",
      "The logarithm is the inverse of the exponential. The logarithm base b of y is the exponent to which b must be raised to give y: log base 10 of 1000 is 3 because 10 cubed is 1000. Logarithms are defined only for positive numbers, and log base b of 1 is 0 for every base.",
      "Logarithms turn multiplication into addition: the log of a product is the sum of the logs, the log of a quotient is the difference, and the log of x to the power n is n times the log of x. That is why logarithmic scales such as decibels and the pH scale compress huge ranges: each step of 1 on a base-10 scale is a factor of 10. The natural logarithm uses the base e, about 2.718."
